fieldsmith 1
# === FIELDSMITH LITERATE CASE ===
# @id: T23
# @code: T23
# @category: tutorial
# @level: Advanced
# @title: Host-Stamped DC04 Clinching S-Lock Co-Design, Optimal X* Dial-In, & 45° Mixed-Peel J2 FEA
# @subtitle: Stamp a parametric 3D S-Lock clinched joint onto a DC04 mild-steel lap coupon via `DocCommand`, evaluate the 51-point Lee–Kim / Breda hat-curve process window, dial residual coin thickness to optimal `X*`, rotate the service load to 45° mixed peel/shear, and verify 3D J2 secant elasto-plastic contracts.
# @verification_badge: Verified by A19 & V63 · Unified Rust Clinching Kernel + 3D J2 Secant FEA
# @fsm_path: examples/tutorials/T23-clinching-process-window-and-slock-codesign.fsm
# @starter_fsm_name: t23-clinching-process-window-and-slock-codesign.fsm
# @verification_refs: docs/verification/V53.md, docs/verification/V63.md, crates/fieldsmith-verify/tests/v63_architecture_lock.rs
# ---
# @mcp: Stamp under-clinched 3D S-Lock joint (X = 1.20 mm) onto DC04 lap coupon with 3D J2 plasticity || apply_clinching || {"insert_joint":true,"host_id":"sheet","bottom_thickness_x_mm":1.20,"service_load_n":2200.0,"j2_plasticity":true,"bottom_x_std_mm":0.04}
# @mcp: Evaluate 51-point Lee-Kim / Breda hat-curve process window and springback-adjusted interlock || evaluate_clinching || {}
# @mcp: Dial coin thickness automatically to optimal X* and rotate load to 45 deg mixed peel || apply_clinching || {"dial_optimal_x":true,"load_angle_deg":45.0}
# @mcp: Verify 3D J2 secant stress and deflection contracts on dialed DC04 S-Lock joint || verify || {"dofs":12000}
# ---
# @assert: DC04 clinch neck J2 von Mises flow stress active || max_vm_elem || >= 20.0 || >= 20.0 || MPa
# @assert: DC04 clinch coupon mixed-peel deflection bounded || max_displacement || <= 2.5 || <= 2.5 || mm
# ---
# @step: 1. Stamp 3D S-Lock Joint & Inspect Hat-Curve Process Window || results
#   Starting from the clamped DC04 lap stack (`sheet`), `apply_clinching` stamps `clinch_slock` (`clinch_die_button` + `clinch_upper_boss`) and subtractive `clinch_recess` (`clinch_die_ring_groove` + `clinch_punch_pit` with `height = 3.8 - X`), binds `clinch_pull` on `clinch_pull_ring`, and enables `solve plasticity=j2`.
# @expected:
#   In **Results (3)**, the **Sheet-Metal Clinching Explorer** plots `F_neck(X)`, `F_pull(X)`, and `X* = 0.78 mm` directly from `fieldsmith-doc::clinching` via WASM.
# @step: 2. Dial Optimal X* & Test 45° Mixed Peel in 3D J2 Secant FEA || results
#   Click **`✨ Dial X*`** (`dial_optimal_x: true`) and **`45° Mixed Peel`** (`load_angle_deg: 45`). Both the browser UI and MCP `apply_clinching` dispatch `DocCommand::ApplyClinching`, updating `let X`, recomputing `clinch_punch_pit.height`, and rotating the 3D force vector to `(F sin 45°, 0, F cos 45°)`.
# @expected:
#   Both `.fsm` `assert` contracts pass under 3D P2 J2 secant elasto-plasticity, and `Undo` restores the prior coin thickness and load angle in one step.
# === END LITERATE HEADER ===

name "DC04 Lap Sheet for S-Lock Clinching Co-Design"
material mat_dc04

box sheet size=(40, 26, 3.0) at=(0, 0, 1.5)

region clamp_edges = sheet.nx + sheet.px
support fixture clamp_edges fixed=xyz

solve build=(0, 0)

assert "DC04 clinch neck J2 von Mises flow stress active" metric="max_vm_elem" target=">= 20.0" tol=">= 20.0" unit="MPa"
assert "DC04 clinch coupon mixed-peel deflection bounded" metric="max_displacement" target="<= 2.5" tol="<= 2.5" unit="mm"
